entor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUNO, YOSHIMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOMURA, TOSHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGAWA, TETSUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATOU, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A composite hardened material characterized by containing an amorphous material (2) consisting of at least two kinds of oxides and having a fibrous material (3) mixed in the amorphous material (2); and a production method thereof, the composite hardened material including one formed by hardening papermaking sludge, whereby enhancing a bending strength without compromise in processibility and productivity.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un matériau composite durci qui se caractérise en ce qu'il contient un matériau amorphe (2) constitué d'au moins deux sortes d'oxydes ainsi qu'un matériau fibreux (3) mélangé audit matériau amorphe (2). L'invention se rapporte également à un procédé de production d'un tel matériau composite durci pouvant consister notamment à durcir une pâte à papier, ce qui permet d'obtenir une résistance accrue à la flexion du matériau sans pour autant réduire ni son aptitude au traitement, ni la productivité.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-faci